ashani and minari are trying to stay on  top of their schoolwork  the sisters who attend a government  school in colombo have public exams in a  few months  but their teachers have stopped  conducting online classes as part of a  trade union action demanding better pay  it's difficult to study the syllabus by  ourselves there's a lot to cover  especially with the final exams coming  the girl's mother sita works as a maid  three days a week their father is a  builder  they say they cannot afford to pay  private tuition for any of their four  children  it's families like us day wage earners  that are the worst affected we only have  school or online classes to rely on  that's why we're worried  sri lanka's ceylon teachers union is on  an indefinite strike which keeps them  away from online teaching exam  preparation paper correction and other  duties  it says 25 years of waiting for better  pay is more than enough  the lowest paid teachers in south asia  are in sri lanka this is truly an  embarrassing situation india salaries  are more than double those paid here we  say increase our salaries immediately  the government won't do anything about  it we will continue our struggle till  they do  successive reviews have agreed that the  salary disparity between teachers and  other government employees must be  addressed  but the government says teachers will  have to wait for the proper procedure to  get the wage hike  the procedure is the budget we've  already begun to make plans to present  the necessary documents as part of the  budget this issue has to be resolved  through the budget and be presented in  that framework  but the teachers are not buying it they  say the government is spending millions  of dollars on unnecessary projects and  can easily sort out the teacher salary  issue if there is a will to do so  recent weeks have seen some of the  largest demonstrations by the 250 000  strong union  heavy-handed police action during the  coronavirus pandemic to arrest and  quarantine protesters has drawn  criticism from the teachers and  affiliated trade unions  the government is trying to suppress us  we will not be coward and we will take  our struggle forward  while the government fights teachers on  salary differences that have lasted for  decades students in over ten thousand  government schools like the one behind  me bear the brunt of the work stoppage  students like ashani and minari will be  hoping the strike will be over soon so  they can carry on with their studies  milo fernandez al jazeera colombo
 

